$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Amide Compounds II. General
Procedure C. To a flame-dried flask were added the carboxylic acid (1.0
equiv), dicyclohexylcarbodiimide (1.1 equiv), dimethylaminopyridine (1.1
equiv), dodecylamine (1.0 equiv), and CH2Cl2 (0.40 M). After stirring at
room temperature for 24 h, the reaction mixture was filtered through a
Celite plug and concentrated. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography. 4-aminopyridine-C4-3-bromophenoxyhybrid (S37): Prepared
from 4-aminopyridine and S36 1 using general procedure C to furnish S37
in a 75% yield. HRMS (ESI-TOF) calculated for C15H16BrN2O2 [M+H]+: m/z
335.0395, found 335.0388; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.59- 8.39 (m, 2H),
8.23 (s, 1H), 7.49 (d, J = 5.4 Hz, 2H), 7.12 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.07
(d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.03-6.99 (m, 1H), 6.78 (dd, J = 8.2, 2.4 Hz, 1H),
4.02 (t, J = 5.8 Hz, 2H), 2.61 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 2.27- 2.14 (m, 2H);
13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.4, 159.3, 150.5, 145.1, 130.6, 124.0,
122.8, 117.7, 113.5, 113.2, 66.8, 33.9, 24.5.
